            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Setting Up",
            "text": "<p><strong>Assembling the Guide Bar and Chain</strong></p><p><strong>Watch the video below for step-by-step instructions on how to assemble the guide bar and chain on the LawnMaster 24v chainsaw.</strong></p><p>1. Lie the chainsaw on a level surface.</p><p>2. Turn the locking knob anti-clockwise to remove the chain cover.</p><p>3. Spread out the saw chain in a loop so that the cutting edges are aligned in a clockwise direction.</p><p>4.Fit the chain around the guide bar ensuring that the direction of the chain is correct  as per the manual.</p><p>5. Align the guide bar and saw chain assembly with the support bolt and drive sprocket on the product. Place the guide bar on the support bolt and lay the saw chain around the drive sprocket.</p><p>6. To assemble, hold the guide bar tilted upwards at an angle of approx. 45 degrees in order to be guide the saw chain more easily onto the drive sprocket. It is normal for the saw chain to sag.</p><p>7. Pre-tension the saw chain by turning the tensioning plate in a clockwise direction.</p><p>8. Replace the chain cover.  Make sure the lug on the cover is first placed in</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
